                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "In the background, it was mentioned that  - expectation is that LogEntry resources expose a section by section decoded CPER instance - would this mean bmcweb would have to Call `Read` , parse it via libcper API's to expose section by section information ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/cper-repository.md",
                    "line": 78,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "I copied the background from @ed@tanous.net previous design doc on cper...I can tweak that if it is confusing the way it is now.  To start with I just wanted to get the attachment in additionalDataUri working.\n\nIf we later want to fill in the cper properties in the logentry, your proposal would work.  We could also have this new application parse it and populate some new dbus properties on this interface."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/cper-repository.md",
                    "line": 90,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "ManojKiran Eda",
                        "email": "manojkiran.eda@gmail.com",
                        "username": "manojkiraneda"
                    },
                    "message": "The problem domain ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/cper-repository.md",
                    "line": 90,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Actually it should be \"it's problem domain\" where it = phosphor-debug-collector.  Nice catch.  Will fix."
                },
